To mock `request.state` in FastAPI tests, you can use the `monkeypatch` fixture from `pytest` to set up a mock object for `request.state`. This can be done by creating a pytest decorator or fixture that allows state to be set up in tests. 

For example, you can create a fixture that sets up a mock `request.state` object and then use it in your tests:

```python
@pytest.fixture
def mock_request_state():
    class MockRequestState:
        def __init__(self, value):
            self.value = value

    return MockRequestState("mocked state")
```

Then, in your test, you can use this fixture to set up the mock `request.state` object:

```python
@pytest.mark.anyio
async def test_default_state(mock_request_state):
    async with AsyncClient(transport=ASGITransport(app=app), base_url="http://example.com") as c:
        res =  await c.get("/")
        assert res.text == str(mock_request_state.value)
```

